{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And He said: Hew for yourself.</b> Like לְךָ לְךָ (Genesis 12:1) and וְאַתָּה קַח־לְךָ (above, Exodus 30:23)." "<b>And the meaning of 'like the first ones.'</b> As is their measure, the Gaon [Saadia] said that the second ones are more honored than the first ones, for the second ones were given on a holy day and on Yom HaKippurim, but not so the first ones, for they came down on the seventeenth of Tammuz and on a weekday, and with the second ones there is mention of three covenants, and in the second ones it is written לְמַעַן יִיטַב לָךְ (Deuteronomy 5:16), and the first ones were shattered, and these [arguments] are like words of a dream — neither to be raised nor lowered, for both were the writing of Elohim, and furthermore the first ones were the work of Elohim and the second ones the work of Moses."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:08.682707692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}